{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"radio-bus","name":"LoRa radio, CAN bus and RS485","version":"1.0.1","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Talking further and tougher: a LoRa radio (SX1278, long range, slow; LoRa.h), a CAN bus module (MCP2515 + TJA1050, as in cars; mcp_can.h) and an RS485 transceiver (MAX485, long wires in noisy places, with Serial). Radios on the same frequency and settings hear each other; CAN and RS485 modules talk over their wires.","category":"Communication","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// LoRa radios, CAN bus modules, RS485 transceivers.\n// LoRa and CAN talk to their sketch libraries (LoRa.h, mcp_can.h) over SPI with a few commands of\n// their own (the libraries hide them: sketches use the usual calls).\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ LoRa\n// Every LoRa radio on the bench: a packet goes to every other one tuned the same way, after its air\n// time (how long the packet takes to send at its spreading factor and bandwidth).\nconst loras = new Set();\nconst BW = [7800, 10400, 15600, 20800, 31250, 41700, 62500, 125000, 250000, 500000];\nconst airtimeMs = (sf, bw, len) => {\n  const tsym = (2 ** sf) / bw * 1000;\n  const low = tsym > 16 ? 1 : 0;\n  const payload = 8 + Math.max(Math.ceil((8 * len - 4 * sf + 28 + 16) / (4 * (sf - 2 * low))) * 5, 0);\n  return (12.25 + payload) * tsym;\n};\nbench.device('lora', (part) => {\n  const r = { powered: false, freq: 0, sf: 7, bw: 125000, sync: 0x12, inbox: [], current: null, sent: 0, got: 0, missed: 0, busyUntil: 0, now: 0 };\n  loras.add(r);\n  const send = (data) => {\n    const t = airtimeMs(r.sf, r.bw, data.length);\n    r.busyUntil = r.now + t / 1000;\n    r.sent++;\n    for (const o of loras) {\n      if (o === r || !o.powered) continue;\n      // tuned the same way: it hears it; a different spreading factor or sync word: it doesn't\n      if (Math.abs(o.freq - r.freq) > 50000 || o.sf !== r.sf || o.bw !== r.bw || o.sync !== r.sync) { o.missed++; continue; }\n      if (o.inbox.length < 8) o.inbox.push({ data, at: r.now + t / 1000, rssi: -48 - Math.round(Math.random() * 6), snr: 9 });\n    }\n    return t;\n  };\n  return {\n    spi: {\n      transfer(bytes) {\n        if (!r.powered) return bytes.map(() => 0);\n        const c = bytes[0];\n        const out = new Array(bytes.length).fill(0);\n        if (c === 0xb0) out[1] = 0x12; // the chip's version: \"it's there\"\n        else if (c === 0xb1) r.freq = ((bytes[1] << 24) >>> 0) + (bytes[2] << 16) + (bytes[3] << 8) + bytes[4];\n        else if (c === 0xb2) { r.sf = Math.max(6, Math.min(12, bytes[1])); r.bw = BW[bytes[2]] ?? 125000; r.sync = bytes[3]; }\n        else if (c === 0xb3) { const n = bytes[1]; const t = send(bytes.slice(2, 2 + n)); out[1] = Math.min(255, Math.ceil(t / 10)); } // (its air time, in 10 ms)\n        else if (c === 0xb4) { // the next packet that has arrived\n          const i = r.inbox.findIndex((p) => p.at <= r.now);\n          r.current = i >= 0 ? r.inbox.splice(i, 1)[0] : null;\n          if (r.current) r.got++;\n          out[1] = r.current ? r.current.data.length : 0;\n        } else if (c === 0xb5) { const d = r.current?.data ?? []; for (let i = 1; i < bytes.length; i++) out[i] = d[i - 1] ?? 0; }\n        else if (c === 0xb6) { out[1] = (r.current?.rssi ?? -120) + 164; out[2] = ((r.current?.snr ?? 0) * 4) & 255; }\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      r.now = io.time;\n      r.powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 2.4 && io.level('RST') !== 0;\n      // DIO0: HIGH while a received packet waits (as \"RxDone\")\n      io.drive('DIO0', r.powered && r.inbox.some((p) => p.at <= r.now) ? io.supply('VCC', 'GND') : 0, 1);\n      io.draw(!r.powered ? 0 : r.now < r.busyUntil ? 0.12 : 0.011); // (sending: ~120 mA; listening: ~11 mA)\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!r.powered) return ['no power (3.3 V)'];\n      if (!r.freq) return ['powered: waiting for LoRa.begin()'];\n      return [`${(r.freq / 1e6).toFixed(1)} MHz, SF${r.sf}, ${r.bw / 1000} kHz${r.now < r.busyUntil ? ', sending...' : ''}`, `${r.sent} sent, ${r.got} received${r.missed ? `, ${r.missed} not heard (other settings)` : ''}`];\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ CAN\n// A frame goes out on CANH as a message; every module on that wire takes it, if it runs at the same\n// speed (at another speed it hears noise). Frame bytes: speed (kbps / 5), ext, id (4), len, data.\nbench.device('mcp2515', (part) => {\n  let powered = false, speed = 0, mode = 0, sent = 0, got = 0, garbled = 0;\n  const rx = [];\n  let outbox = [];\n  const crystal = Number(part.params.crystal) || 8;\n  return {\n    spi: {\n      transfer(bytes) {\n        if (!powered) return bytes.map(() => 0);\n        const c = bytes[0];\n        const out = new Array(bytes.length).fill(0);\n        if (c === 0xc0) { // begin: speed (kbps / 5), the crystal the sketch says, mode\n          const asked = bytes[1] * 5, said = bytes[2];\n          // a sketch that names the wrong crystal runs at the wrong speed (half or double)\n          speed = said && said !== crystal ? asked * (crystal / said) : asked;\n          out[1] = 0x55;\n        } else if (c === 0xc4) mode = bytes[1];\n        else if (c === 0xc1) {\n          if (mode === 0x40) rx.push({ id: bytes.slice(2, 6), ext: bytes[1], data: bytes.slice(7, 7 + bytes[6]) }); // loopback\n          else outbox.push([Math.round(speed / 5) & 255, ...bytes.slice(1, 7 + bytes[6])]);\n          sent++;\n        } else if (c === 0xc2) out[1] = rx.length;\n        else if (c === 0xc3) {\n          const f = rx.shift();\n          if (f) { out[1] = f.ext; f.id.forEach((b, i) => (out[2 + i] = b)); out[6] = f.data.length; f.data.forEach((b, i) => (out[7 + i] = b)); }\n        }\n        return out;\n      },\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 4.2;\n      for (const f of outbox) io.send('CANH', 'data', f);\n      outbox = [];\n      io.drive('INT', powered && rx.length ? 0 : io.supply('VCC', 'GND'), 1);\n      io.draw(powered ? 0.012 + (sent ? 0.01 : 0) : 0);\n    },\n    packets(list) {\n      for (const p of list) {\n        if (p.pin !== 'CANH' || p.proto !== 'data' || !powered || mode === 0x40) continue;\n        const [sp, ext, a, b, c, d, len, ...data] = p.data;\n        if (Math.abs(sp * 5 - speed) > 1) { garbled++; continue; } // (a different speed: noise, ignored)\n        if (rx.length < 16) { rx.push({ ext, id: [a, b, c, d], data: data.slice(0, len) }); got++; }\n      }\n    },\n    status: () => [!powered ? 'no power (5 V)' : !speed ? 'waiting for CAN0.begin()' : `${speed} kbps${mode === 0x40 ? ' (loopback)' : ''}`, `${sent} sent, ${got} received${garbled ? `, ${garbled} at another speed (ignored)` : ''}`],\n  };\n});\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ RS485\n// DE HIGH: what the board sends on DI goes out on A/B; RE LOW: what comes in on A/B goes to RO.\nbench.device('max485', (part) => {\n  let powered = false, de = false, re = false, sent = 0, got = 0, garbled = 0;\n  let pending = [];\n  return {\n    step(io) {\n      powered = io.supply('VCC', 'GND') >= 4.2;\n      de = io.level('DE') === 1;\n      re = io.level('RE') === 0;\n      for (const [pin, data, baud] of pending) io.send(pin, 'uart', data, baud);\n      pending = [];\n      if (!re) io.drive('RO', io.supply('VCC', 'GND'), 0); else io.release('RO');\n      io.draw(powered ? (de ? 0.06 : 0.0005) : 0);\n    },\n    packets(list) {\n      if (!powered) return;\n      for (const p of list) {\n        if (p.proto !== 'uart') continue;\n        if (p.pin === 'DI' && de) { pending.push(['A', p.data, p.baud]); sent += p.data.length; if (re) pending.push(['RO', p.data, p.baud]); }\n        else if ((p.pin === 'A' || p.pin === 'B') && re) {\n          // wired A to B (swapped): the line's levels are upside down, the bytes come out wrong\n          const data = p.pin === 'A' ? p.data : p.data.map((b) => ~b & 255);\n          if (p.pin === 'B') garbled += data.length; else got += data.length;\n          pending.push(['RO', data, p.baud]);\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    status: () => [!powered ? 'no power (5 V)' : `${de ? 'sending' : 'not sending'}, ${re ? 'receiving' : 'not receiving'}`, `${sent} bytes out, ${got} in${garbled ? `, ${garbled} garbled (A and B swapped?)` : ''}`],\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"LoRa.h":{"classes":["LoRaClass"],"exports":["LoRa"],"code":"// LoRa.h (Sandeep Mistry's library), the parts most sketches use:\n//   LoRa.setPins(ss, reset, dio0);  if (!LoRa.begin(433E6)) { ... }\n//   LoRa.beginPacket(); LoRa.print(\"hello\"); LoRa.write(b); LoRa.endPacket();\n//   int n = LoRa.parsePacket(); while (LoRa.available()) char c = LoRa.read(); LoRa.readString();\n//   LoRa.packetRssi(); LoRa.packetSnr(); LoRa.setSpreadingFactor(7..12); LoRa.setSignalBandwidth(125E3);\n//   LoRa.setSyncWord(0x12); LoRa.setTxPower(17); LoRa.idle(); LoRa.sleep();\n// (It talks to the radio over SPI; endPacket() waits the packet's real air time.)\nclass LoRaClass {\n  constructor() { this.ss = typeof SS === 'number' ? SS : 10; this.rst = -1; this.dio0 = -1; this.tx = []; this.rxb = []; this.rssi = -120; this.snr = 0; this.sf = 7; this.bw = 7; this.sync = 0x12; this.ok = false; }\n  _x(bytes) { digitalWrite(this.ss, LOW); const r = SPI.transfer(bytes.slice()); digitalWrite(this.ss, HIGH); return r; }\n  setPins(ss = 10, reset = 9, dio0 = 2) { this.ss = ss; this.rst = reset; this.dio0 = dio0; }\n  setSPIFrequency() {}\n  begin(freq) {\n    pinMode(this.ss, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.ss, HIGH);\n    if (this.rst >= 0) { pinMode(this.rst, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.rst, LOW); delay(10); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(10); }\n    SPI.begin();\n    if (this._x([0xb0, 0])[1] !== 0x12) return 0; // (no radio answers: wiring, or no 3.3 V)\n    const f = Math.round(Number(freq)) >>> 0;\n    this._x([0xb1, (f >>> 24) & 255, (f >>> 16) & 255, (f >>> 8) & 255, f & 255]);\n    this._cfg();\n    this.ok = true;\n    return 1;\n  }\n  end() { this.ok = false; }\n  _cfg() { this._x([0xb2, this.sf, this.bw, this.sync]); }\n  setSpreadingFactor(sf) { this.sf = Math.max(6, Math.min(12, sf | 0)); this._cfg(); }\n  setSignalBandwidth(bw) { const list = [7.8e3, 10.4e3, 15.6e3, 20.8e3, 31.25e3, 41.7e3, 62.5e3, 125e3, 250e3, 500e3]; let i = list.findIndex((b) => bw <= b); if (i < 0) i = 9; this.bw = i; this._cfg(); }\n  setSyncWord(sw) { this.sync = sw & 255; this._cfg(); }\n  setFrequency(freq) { const f = Math.round(Number(freq)) >>> 0; this._x([0xb1, (f >>> 24) & 255, (f >>> 16) & 255, (f >>> 8) & 255, f & 255]); }\n  setTxPower() {} setCodingRate4() {} setPreambleLength() {} enableCrc() {} disableCrc() {} idle() {} sleep() {} receive() {}\n  onReceive() { warn('LoRa.onReceive: on the bench, call LoRa.parsePacket() in loop() instead (callbacks aren\\'t supported)'); }\n  beginPacket() { this.tx = []; return 1; }\n  write(b, n) {\n    if (typeof b === 'object' && b && typeof b.length === 'number') { const k = n ?? b.length; for (let i = 0; i < k; i++) this.tx.push((typeof b[i] === 'string' ? b[i].charCodeAt(0) : b[i]) & 255); return k; }\n    this.tx.push(Number(b) & 255); return 1;\n  }\n  print(x, fmt) {\n    const s = typeof x === 'number' && fmt !== undefined ? (fmt === 16 ? x.toString(16).toUpperCase() : x.toFixed(fmt)) : typeof x === 'number' && !Number.isInteger(x) ? x.toFixed(2) : String(x);\n    for (const ch of s) this.tx.push(ch.charCodeAt(0) & 255);\n    return s.length;\n  }\n  println(x = '') { const n = this.print(x); this.tx.push(13, 10); return n + 2; }\n  endPacket() {\n    if (!this.ok) return 0;\n    const data = this.tx.slice(0, 255);\n    const r = this._x([0xb3, data.length, ...data]);\n    delay(r[1] * 10); // (the real air time: sending waits for it)\n    this.tx = [];\n    return 1;\n  }\n  parsePacket() {\n    if (!this.ok) return 0;\n    const n = this._x([0xb4, 0])[1];\n    if (!n) return 0;\n    this.rxb = this._x([0xb5, ...new Array(n).fill(0)]).slice(1, 1 + n);\n    const q = this._x([0xb6, 0, 0]);\n    this.rssi = q[1] - 164;\n    this.snr = (q[2] > 127 ? q[2] - 256 : q[2]) / 4;\n    return n;\n  }\n  available() { return this.rxb.length; }\n  read() { return this.rxb.length ? this.rxb.shift() : -1; }\n  peek() { return this.rxb.length ? this.rxb[0] : -1; }\n  readString() { let s = ''; while (this.rxb.length) s += String.fromCharCode(this.rxb.shift()); return s; }\n  packetRssi() { return this.rssi; }\n  packetSnr() { return this.snr; }\n  rssi() { return -110; }\n}\nconst LoRa = new LoRaClass();\n"},"mcp_can.h":{"classes":["MCP_CAN"],"exports":["CAN_OK","CAN_FAILINIT","CAN_FAILTX","CAN_MSGAVAIL","CAN_NOMSG","CAN_CTRLERROR","CAN_GETTXBFTIMEOUT","CAN_SENDMSGTIMEOUT","CAN_FAIL","MCP_ANY","MCP_STD","MCP_EXT","MCP_STDEXT","MCP_NORMAL","MCP_SLEEP","MCP_LOOPBACK","MCP_LISTENONLY","MCP_8MHZ","MCP_16MHZ","MCP_20MHZ","CAN_5KBPS","CAN_10KBPS","CAN_20KBPS","CAN_50KBPS","CAN_100KBPS","CAN_125KBPS","CAN_250KBPS","CAN_500KBPS","CAN_1000KBPS"],"code":"// mcp_can.h (Cory Fowler's library), the parts most sketches use:\n//   MCP_CAN CAN0(10);  CAN0.begin(MCP_ANY, CAN_500KBPS, MCP_8MHZ) == CAN_OK;  CAN0.setMode(MCP_NORMAL);\n//   byte data[8] = {...};  CAN0.sendMsgBuf(0x100, 0, 8, data);   (0 = standard id, 1 = extended)\n//   if (CAN0.checkReceive() == CAN_MSGAVAIL) { CAN0.readMsgBuf(&rxId, &len, rxBuf); }\n//   (or watch the module's INT pin: LOW while a message waits)\nconst CAN_OK = 0, CAN_FAILINIT = 1, CAN_FAILTX = 2, CAN_MSGAVAIL = 3, CAN_NOMSG = 4, CAN_CTRLERROR = 5, CAN_GETTXBFTIMEOUT = 6, CAN_SENDMSGTIMEOUT = 7, CAN_FAIL = 0xff;\nconst MCP_ANY = 0, MCP_STD = 1, MCP_EXT = 2, MCP_STDEXT = 3;\nconst MCP_NORMAL = 0x00, MCP_SLEEP = 0x20, MCP_LOOPBACK = 0x40, MCP_LISTENONLY = 0x60;\nconst MCP_8MHZ = 8, MCP_16MHZ = 16, MCP_20MHZ = 20;\nconst CAN_5KBPS = 5, CAN_10KBPS = 10, CAN_20KBPS = 20, CAN_50KBPS = 50, CAN_100KBPS = 100, CAN_125KBPS = 125, CAN_250KBPS = 250, CAN_500KBPS = 500, CAN_1000KBPS = 1000;\nclass MCP_CAN {\n  constructor(cs = 10) { this.cs = cs; this.ok = false; }\n  _x(bytes) { digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW); const r = SPI.transfer(bytes.slice()); digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH); return r; }\n  begin(idmode, speed, clock) {\n    pinMode(this.cs, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\n    SPI.begin();\n    const r = this._x([0xc0, Math.round(Number(speed) / 5) & 255, Number(clock) & 255, 0]);\n    this.ok = r[1] === 0x55;\n    return this.ok ? CAN_OK : CAN_FAILINIT;\n  }\n  setMode(m) { this._x([0xc4, m & 255]); return CAN_OK; }\n  init_Mask() { return CAN_OK; } init_Filt() { return CAN_OK; }\n  sendMsgBuf(id, ext, len, buf) {\n    if (buf === undefined) { buf = len; len = ext; ext = id > 0x7ff ? 1 : 0; } // (sendMsgBuf(id, len, buf))\n    if (!this.ok) return CAN_FAILTX;\n    const n = Math.max(0, Math.min(8, len | 0));\n    const data = [];\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) data.push((typeof buf[i] === 'string' ? buf[i].charCodeAt(0) : Number(buf[i] ?? 0)) & 255);\n    const v = Number(id) >>> 0;\n    this._x([0xc1, ext ? 1 : 0, (v >>> 24) & 255, (v >>> 16) & 255, (v >>> 8) & 255, v & 255, n, ...data]);\n    return CAN_OK;\n  }\n  checkReceive() { return this.ok && this._x([0xc2, 0])[1] ? CAN_MSGAVAIL : CAN_NOMSG; }\n  readMsgBuf(id, len, buf) {\n    const r = this._x([0xc3, ...new Array(15).fill(0)]);\n    const n = r[6];\n    const v = ((r[2] << 24) >>> 0) + (r[3] << 16) + (r[4] << 8) + r[5];\n    // (as the real library: an extended id comes back with bit 31 set)\n    const full = r[1] ? (v | 0x80000000) >>> 0 : v;\n    if (isRef(id)) id.value = full;\n    if (isRef(len)) len.value = n;\n    for (let i = 0; i < n && buf && i < 8; i++) buf[i] = r[7 + i];\n    return n ? CAN_OK : CAN_NOMSG;\n  }\n  checkError() { return CAN_OK; }\n  getError() { return 0; }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"lora","name":"LoRa radio (SX1278, 433 MHz)","description":"Long-range, slow radio (kilometres outdoors; a few hundred bytes a second). SPI: SCK, MISO, MOSI, NSS (its CS), plus RST and DIO0. 3.3 V only. With #include <LoRa.h>: LoRa.setPins(ss, rst, dio0); LoRa.begin(433E6); LoRa.beginPacket(); LoRa.print(\"hi\"); LoRa.endPacket(); and on the other one: int n = LoRa.parsePacket(); if (n) while (LoRa.available()) Serial.print((char)LoRa.read()). Sending takes the real air time (SF7, 125 kHz: about 50 ms for 20 bytes; SF12: over a second). Two radios hear each other only with the same frequency, spreading factor, bandwidth and sync word.","swatch":"#2e7d4f","mass":3,"shape":[{"box":[2.77,0.16,2.04],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2e7d4f"},{"box":[1.7,0.25,1.6],"at":[-0.3,0.28,-0.15],"color":"#b9bec7","collide":false},{"cyl":[0.15,1.2],"at":[1.1,0.75,-0.7],"color":"#d9b54a","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","MISO","MOSI","SCK","NSS","RST","DIO0","VCC"],"at":[-0.889,0.16,0.87],"dir":"x","kinds":{"GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin","MISO":"out","MOSI":"in","SCK":"in","NSS":"in","RST":"in","DIO0":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3 V only)","vmin":2.4,"vmax":3.7},"NSS":{"label":"NSS (CS)","pulled":"up"},"RST":{"pulled":"up"}}}],"spi":{"sck":"SCK","mosi":"MOSI","miso":"MISO","cs":"NSS"},"device":"lora"},{"id":"mcp2515","name":"CAN bus module (MCP2515 + TJA1050)","description":"Joins a board to a CAN bus (the two-wire network in cars and machines): wire every module's CANH together and every CANL together. SPI to the board: SCK, SI (MOSI), SO (MISO), CS; INT goes LOW while a message waits. 5 V. With #include <mcp_can.h>: MCP_CAN CAN0(10); CAN0.begin(MCP_ANY, CAN_500KBPS, MCP_8MHZ) == CAN_OK; CAN0.setMode(MCP_NORMAL); CAN0.sendMsgBuf(0x100, 0, 8, data); and if (CAN0.checkReceive() == CAN_MSGAVAIL) CAN0.readMsgBuf(&id, &len, buf). Every module on a bus must use the same speed.","swatch":"#2a62c8","mass":6,"params":[{"key":"crystal","label":"Its crystal","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"8","label":"8 MHz (most blue modules)"},{"value":"16","label":"16 MHz"}]}],"defaults":{"crystal":"8"},"shape":[{"box":[4.4,0.16,2.8],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2a62c8"},{"box":[0.9,0.12,1.2],"at":[-0.3,0.22,0],"color":"#151618","collide":false},{"box":[1,0.9,0.9],"at":[1.7,0.61,0],"color":"#2a62f0"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["INT","SCK","SI","SO","CS","GND","VCC"],"at":[-2.05,0.16,-0.762],"dir":"z","kinds":{"INT":"out","SCK":"in","SI":"in","SO":"out","CS":"in","GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (5 V)","vmin":4.5,"vmax":5.5},"CS":{"pulled":"up"},"INT":{"label":"INT (LOW: a message waits)"}}}],"pins":[{"id":"CANH","label":"CANH","at":[2,1.1,-0.25],"kind":"io"},{"id":"CANL","label":"CANL","at":[2,1.1,0.25],"kind":"io"}],"spi":{"sck":"SCK","mosi":"SI","miso":"SO","cs":"CS"},"device":"mcp2515"},{"id":"max485","name":"RS485 transceiver (MAX485)","description":"Serial over long twisted wires (up to 1200 m), many devices on one pair. Board side: DI (the board's TX), RO (its RX), DE (HIGH: send) and RE (LOW: receive), usually tied together on one pin. Line side: A to A, B to B on every module (swapped, the bytes come out garbled). Use Serial1 / Serial2 / SoftwareSerial at the same baud on every node; set DE/RE HIGH just while sending.","swatch":"#2a62c8","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[4.4,0.16,1.4],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#2a62c8"},{"box":[0.6,0.12,0.5],"at":[0,0.22,0],"color":"#151618","collide":false},{"box":[0.8,1,1],"at":[1.4,0.66,0],"color":"#2e7d4f"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["RO","RE","DE","DI"],"at":[-2,0.16,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"RO":"out","RE":"in","DE":"in","DI":"in"},"extra":{"RE":{"label":"RE (LOW: receive)"},"DE":{"label":"DE (HIGH: send)"}}},{"ids":["VCC","B","A","GND"],"at":[2,0.16,-0.381],"dir":"z","kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","A":"io","B":"io"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (5 V)","vmin":4.5,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"max485"}],"examples":[]}